<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48976" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trĭangŭlus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		tres-angulus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>having three corners</i> or <i>angles</i>, <i>threecornered</i>, <i>triangular.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sidera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 2, 42, 89</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">forma cutis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					7, 25, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">species (Siciliae),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 8, 14, § 86</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					5, 2, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">latera radicis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 13, 11, 218</span></i>
			 et saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Substt.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trĭangŭlum</span></b> , i,
			n., <i>a triangle</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quadrata amplius spatium complectuntur
					triangulis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 10, 41</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">id. 1, 10, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. N.
				D. 2, 49, 125</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 27, 8, 39, §
			61</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trĭangŭlus</span></b> , i,
			m., <i>a triangle</i>, Front. Expos. Form.
			pp. 32, 33, 35 Goes.</div>
